    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0430" n="416" xml:id="pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/12–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-07T20:00:00-04:00">December 7, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10249. We regret that we have not been able to send a reply to the request made
                    in the last paragraph of your 10609 of December 1 (Comea 132). The Working
                    Security Committee promptly held several meetings on this subject but because of
                    differences of opinion which developed between the military representatives was
                    unable to agree upon a reply. We are still working on this question and it will
                    be discussed in a high level conference tomorrow. We shall advise you of action
                    here at the earliest possible moment.</p>
                <p>In the meantime, it is suggested that you agree to the establishment of a
                    subcommittee of EAC to consider this question and cable any developments in that
                    subcommittee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
